 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Yes, one day is usually one hundred miles. It can be bit more if you stop and rest, but it' a typical goal for beginners. That's a lot depending on how fit you are now and how fast you ride. A reasonable estimate is one to two hours per hundred miles. Very smart. The metric one is a good choice for beginners, since there are lots of bike trips of that length. Start with one or two hundred mile rides each month, building up to three or four by the time you move on bigger goals.",
